            <ArticleTitle>[Characteristics of Tl-201 myocardial SPECT images of patients with coronary artery lesion of diagonal branch].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>743-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Noninvasive detection of coronary artery lesion of diagonal branch is important. Utility of Tl-201 myocardial SPECT images for this purpose was studied in 9 patients with angina pectoris and 4 patients with myocardial infarction, in whom localized stenosis more than 75% was noted at diagonal branch. Position of basal margin of abnormal region in the coronal images lay between -30 degree and 30 degree and basal abnormal region was very narrow. Width of mid portion of abnormal region lay from 5 degree to 70 degree. Abnormal region due to diagonal branch was not noted in septal region. These results showed the utility of Tl-201 myocardial SPECT images for detecting coronary artery lesion of diagonal branch.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
